# Backend — NestJS Hexagonal + ROP

Every domain service is a **NestJS** application (brief-required framework). Serverless Framework only packages/deploys it.

## Layers (Ports & Adapters inside Nest)

```
domain/          # entities, value objects, domain errors
application/     # use-cases (ROP orchestration)
ports/           # inbound/outbound interfaces
adapters/
  inbound/       # Nest controllers (thin) + filters/pipes
  outbound/      # ElectroDB repos, payment-gateway HTTP client
*.module.ts      # Nest DI wiring (ports → adapters)
lambda.ts        # SF4 Lambda entry bootstrapping NestFactory
```

- Controllers: parse HTTP → call use-case → map `Result` to response. **No business logic.**
- Use-cases are Nest injectable providers depending on **ports** only.

## Railway Oriented Programming

Prefer `Result<T, E>` (or neverthrow) pipelines in use-cases; map failures to HTTP in filters/interceptors — not thrown stacks for expected domain errors.

## Data

- DynamoDB via ElectroDB in outbound adapters only; seed dummy products; document keys in README.
